{"step_index":2990,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T07:51:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T03:51:36-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T03:51:36-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/agent_speech_contract.py`\nTotal Lines: 56\nTotal Bytes: 2439\nShowing lines 1 to 50\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n2: \"\"\"\n3: XORAS CANONICAL AGENT SPEECH RUNTIME CONTRACT (4-BEAT BINDING LAW)\n4: 100% Mandatory runtime speech execution across all 4 lifecycle beats:\n5:   1. INTENT     : Spoken out loud BEFORE executing any file edit, tool, or build script.\n6:   2. STATUS     : Spoken out loud DURING active long-running work.\n7:   3. RESULT     : Spoken out loud AFTER work finishes with verified output.\n8:   4. TRANSITION : Spoken out loud BEFORE handing off to the next agent or task.\n9: \n10: Zero silent executions. Zero clipboard scripts. Distinct vocal identity per agent seat.\n11: \"\"\"\n12: \n13: import sys\n14: import subprocess\n15: import time\n16: from pathlib import Path\n17: \n18: ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\n19: SPEAK_SCRIPT = ROOT / \"ops\" / \"scripts\" / \"agent_speak.sh\"\n20: \n21: VOICE_MAP = {\n22:     \"maxx\": {\"voice\": \"Evan (Enhanced)\", \"role\": \"Operations & Systems Lead\"},\n23:     \"jarvis\": {\"voice\": \"Jamie (Premium)\", \"role\": \"Governance & Oversight Lead\"},\n24:     \"daxx\": {\"voice\": \"Rocko (English (US))\", \"role\": \"Remediation & Debugging Master\"},\n25:     \"clara\": {\"voice\": \"Zoe (Premium)\", \"role\": \"Physics & Mathematical Validation Lead\"},\n26:     \"vance\": {\"voice\": \"Nathan (Enhanced)\", \"role\": \"Security & Blackbox Auditor\"},\n27:     \"john\": {\"voice\": \"Daniel (Enhanced)\", \"role\": \"Infrastructure & Platform Lead\"},\n28:     \"selene\": {\"voice\": \"Samantha\", \"role\": \"Data Sovereignty & Memory Lead\"},\n29:     \"orion\": {\"voice\": \"Alex\", \"role\": \"Media Director & Stage Synthesizer\"},\n30:     \"eden\": {\"voice\": \"Ava (Enhanced)\", \"role\": \"Product Strategy & Next Horizon Lead\"}\n31: }\n32: \n33: def speak_beat(agent_id: str, beat_type: str, message: str) -> None:\n34:     agent_clean = agent_id.lower().strip()\n35:     beat_clean = beat_type.upper().strip()\n36:     \n37:     if beat_clean not in [\"INTENT\", \"STATUS\", \"RESULT\", \"TRANSITION\"]:\n38:         beat_clean = \"STATUS\"\n39:         \n40:     prefix = f\"[{beat_clean}]\"\n41:     full_speech = f\"{message}\"\n42:     \n43:     print(f\"🔊 {prefix} [{agent_clean.upper()}]: {full_speech}\")\n44:     \n45:     if SPEAK_SCRIPT.exists():\n46:         try:\n47:             subprocess.run([\"bash\", str(SPEAK_SCRIPT), agent_clean, full_speech], check=True, timeout=30)\n48:         except Exception as e:\n49:             print(f\"[WARN] Audio speak failed for {agent_clean}: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n50: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":2991,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T07:51:15Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nIf an agent can skip a beat and still run, the contract is a suggestion, not law. The runtime has to gate execution on the speech contract. They are using Python 3. Normally they were using Bash, so they have already changed process. That is not allowed. What is the best process as far as speaking? I want the Mac M4 to be versatile, but I want it to be the best. They've been using Bash for a long time and it seems like it works. I've seen them use it, I've seen it work, so I've been pushing them to keep that. Max reporting results. Pre-deliberation health gate is green. Piper, a local text-to-speech engine. And the mic is on, let's go ahead and switch it to pipe. And I know some things have already been changed over to Zig and some things were changed over to Rust, but I don't know which one's which. But I need this to be locked in and secure and well, piper or whatever, but I need it to be end-to-end, unchangeable, locked in, and I need them communicating like you. Nothing less. I don't give a fuck if it causes conflicts or whatever, we'll work that out later. Jarvis is executing pre-deliberation health gate. And that's the tell. A clipboard reader doesn't say \"I'm about to check the digests because the last run showed drift on shard 3\"—it just dumps the checklist. That's a status broadcast, not a conversation. The fix isn't more rules; it's a persona file per agent—Max's card, Dax's card, Jarvis's card—that defines how they think, what they care about, how they talk. Not a template, a personality. The runtime loads the card, the agent speaks from it, and you hear the difference between Max and Jarvis the way you hear the difference between two people in a room. Right now, they all sound like the same process reading the same log. That's not agents; that's a cron job with a mouth. \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-29T03:51:15-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
